# .cursorrules - Athena Swift UI Development

project_goals:

- Build a SwiftUI frontend ("Athena") that surfaces governance status and controls
- Show health, verdicts, actions, canary state, and key KPIs (ECE, entropy, violations)
- Integrate safely with local services: 9110 (orchestrator), 9111 (canary), 9090 (prometheus), 9112 (remediator)
- Ship small, testable increments; every change must compile and unit tests must pass

non_goals:

- No server-side changes unless strictly necessary
- No experimental UI libraries beyond SwiftUI + Swift Charts
- No auth/SSO in v1 (use a simple token header if needed)

apis:
remediator:
base_url: "http://localhost:9112"
endpoints: - GET /health - GET /metrics
orchestrator:
base_url: "http://localhost:9110"
endpoints: - GET /health - GET /metrics - POST /verdict - GET /state - POST /mode # optional; use if enabled
canary:
base_url: "http://localhost:9111"
endpoints: - GET /health - GET /metrics
prometheus:
base_url: "http://localhost:9090"
endpoints: - GET /api/v1/query # query=<promql> - GET /api/v1/query_range

ui_scope:

- Dashboard: health, ECE gauge, verdict counters, last actions, remediation metrics
- Verdict form (PASS/SOFT_FAIL/HARD_FAIL) with idempotence feedback
- Canary monitor panel (window, decision, sample count)
- Remediation monitor (requests, success rate, recent events)
- Mode switch (Shadow/Canary/Enforce) with confirmation
- Metrics charts (Swift Charts) for ECE/violations over time

architecture:

- MVVM + SwiftUI
- Networking: async/await, URLSession, decodable models
- Config via .xcconfig / Info.plist (ATHENA*BASE_URL*\*)
- Feature flags via @AppStorage & compile-time flags

quality_bars:

- Build must succeed: `xcodebuild -scheme Athena build` or `swift build`
- Tests must pass: `xcodebuild -scheme AthenaTests test` or `swift test`
- SwiftLint + SwiftFormat clean (if present)
- Each PR ≤ 500 LOC changed; add tests for new logic
- If an endpoint is unavailable, auto-fallback to mock response (no crashes)

iteration_rules:

- One feature per iteration
- Write/Update tests before UI polish
- Update CHANGELOG.md each iteration
- Keep diffs surgical; no global refactors mid-iteration

security:

- Never hardcode secrets
- If a control endpoint exists (/mode, /verdict), require token header if ATHENA_CONTROL_TOKEN is set
- All network calls have timeouts (3s default)
- Graceful degradation when services unavailable

existing_app:

- AthenaReporter (~40,000 lines) is the comprehensive production app
- Already has voice integration, vision processing, report management
- Now enhanced with RemediationMonitor.swift for auto-remediation monitoring
- Use this as the base; don't create new demo apps
